From 49d687b21cd6741604a3020dd11ad15c9114d8d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luissalet <luismasc16@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 03:05:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 36/36] Route a ComfyUI connection, and stop promising a
 detailer that is not there
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Three branches landed at once and the seams between them were the work. The
ComfyUI adapter existed but nothing could reach it: the connection kind was not
in the union, the gateway did not route to it, and the IPC handler collapsed
every unrecognised kind to openai-compatible, which would have turned a ComfyUI
connection into one talking the wrong protocol at the right port.

The REQUEST_SUPPORTS table did exactly what it was built to do. Five fields
landed on the request and their  stopped compiling, naming their own
lines. Three of them were checking a name the request does not use, so those
checks now point at the field it actually declares — otherwise this stops being
a compile-time fact and becomes a comment that happens to be true.

The detail pass was refusing with 'the request has no field for this yet', and
that is a promise of a release that is not coming: at the pinned commit the
detailer strings appear nowhere in the parser, the CLI or the public header.
It now says the build has none, the way the upscale pass already did.

quick-note.html is committed because vite.config.ts names it as an entry point
and it was never tracked, so the harness aborted on a cold checkout.
